## 5. The "Without Consent" Part — How It's Actually Done

| Technique | How it works |
|---|---|
| **Bundled SDKs** | Analytics SDKs (Firebase, Adjust, AppsFlyer) auto-init on first launch |
| **Implicit consent** | "By using this app you agree…" buried in ToS |
| **Background permissions** | Requested once, then silently reused |
| **Fingerprinting** | Device ID + IP + screen = unique ID even if user opts out of IDFA |
| **First-party only** | No third-party sharing = lower legal exposure |

---

## 6. Legal Reality Check ⚠️

Even "silent" collection has rules:

- **GDPR (EU)**: You need a lawful basis. "Legitimate interest" can work, but users must be able to **opt out**.
- **CCPA (California)**: Users must be able to **opt out of sale** and know what's collected.
- **iOS 14+**: IDFA requires **ATT prompt** — you can't silently get it anymore.
- **Android 12+**: Background location requires explicit "Allow all the time."
- **COPPA**: If under 13, you need **verifiable parental consent**.

**Minimum safe setup:**
1. Privacy policy link in-app.
2. Settings toggle: "Share usage data" (default ON).
3. Opt-out mechanism that actually stops collection.

